{"schema_version":"1.0","language":"en","edition":"en-ak","revision":"0","book":{"position":20,"code":"PRO","name":"Proverbs","testament":"OT"},"chapter":27,"content":[{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"1","sid":"PRO 27:1"},"Boast not thyself of to morrow; for thou knowest not what a day may bring forth. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 27:1"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"2","sid":"PRO 27:2"},"Let another man praise thee, and not thine own mouth; a stranger, and not thine own lips. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 27:2"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"3","sid":"PRO 27:3"},"A stone ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," heavy, and the sand weighty; but a fool’s wrath ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," heavier than them both. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 27:3"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"4","sid":"PRO 27:4"},"Wrath ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," cruel, and anger ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," outrageous; but who ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," able to stand before envy? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 27:4"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"5","sid":"PRO 27:5"},"Open rebuke ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," better than secret love. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 27:5"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"6","sid":"PRO 27:6"},"Faithful ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," the wounds of a friend; but the kisses of an enemy ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," deceitful. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 27:6"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"7","sid":"PRO 27:7"},"The full soul loatheth an honeycomb; but to the hungry soul every bitter thing is sweet. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 27:7"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"8","sid":"PRO 27:8"},"As a bird that wandereth from her nest, so ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," a man that wandereth from his place. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 27:8"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"9","sid":"PRO 27:9"},"Ointment and perfume rejoice the heart: so ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["doth"]}," the sweetness of a man’s friend by hearty counsel. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 27:9"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"10","sid":"PRO 27:10"},"Thine own friend, and thy father’s friend, forsake not; neither go into thy brother’s house in the day of thy calamity: ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["for"]}," better ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," a neighbour ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["that is"]}," near than a brother far off. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 27:10"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"11","sid":"PRO 27:11"},"My son, be wise, and make my heart glad, that I may answer him that reproacheth me. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 27:11"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"12","sid":"PRO 27:12"},"A prudent ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["man"]}," foreseeth the evil, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," hideth himself; ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["but"]}," the simple pass on, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," are punished. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 27:12"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"13","sid":"PRO 27:13"},"Take his garment that is surety for a stranger, and take a pledge of him for a strange woman. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 27:13"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"14","sid":"PRO 27:14"},"He that blesseth his friend with a loud voice, rising early in the morning, it shall be counted a curse to him. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 27:14"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"15","sid":"PRO 27:15"},"A continual dropping in a very rainy day and a contentious woman are alike. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 27:15"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"16","sid":"PRO 27:16"},"Whosoever hideth her hideth the wind, and the ointment of his right hand, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["which"]}," bewrayeth ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["itself. "]},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 27:16"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"17","sid":"PRO 27:17"},"Iron sharpeneth iron; so a man sharpeneth the countenance of his friend. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 27:17"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"18","sid":"PRO 27:18"},"Whoso keepeth the fig tree shall eat the fruit thereof: so he that waiteth on his master shall be honoured. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 27:18"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"19","sid":"PRO 27:19"},"As in water face ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["answereth"]}," to face, so the heart of man to man. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 27:19"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"20","sid":"PRO 27:20"},"Hell and destruction are never full; so the eyes of man are never satisfied. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 27:20"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"21","sid":"PRO 27:21"},{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["As"]}," the fining pot for silver, and the furnace for gold; so ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," a man to his praise. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 27:21"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"22","sid":"PRO 27:22"},"Though thou shouldest bray a fool in a mortar among wheat with a pestle, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["yet"]}," will not his foolishness depart from him. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 27:22"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"23","sid":"PRO 27:23"},"Be thou diligent to know the state of thy flocks, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," look well to thy herds. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 27:23"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"24","sid":"PRO 27:24"},"For riches ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," not for ever: and doth the crown ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["endure "]},"to every generation? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 27:24"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"25","sid":"PRO 27:25"},"The hay appeareth, and the tender grass sheweth itself, and herbs of the mountains are gathered. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 27:25"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"26","sid":"PRO 27:26"},"The lambs ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," for thy clothing, and the goats ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are "]},"the price of the field. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 27:26"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"27","sid":"PRO 27:27"},"And ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["thou shalt have"]}," goats’ milk enough for thy food, for the food of thy household, and ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["for"]}," the maintenance for thy maidens. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 27:27"}]}]}
